3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p-MC(Φ)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">Φ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is computable in polynomial time.</strong> An IMP+ program reads the word,\nskips the structure using its header (the number of symbols, the arities, the size, then per symbol\nthe number of tuples, each block being that number times the arity long), and walks the prefix code\nof the formula to the end of the word, adding up the contribution of each tag; it runs in\n<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">O(|x|)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> steps."},"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized.html","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized:assumption:Lax496464.WH_A5_Bridges:0","e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.pWD_isParameterized:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"","nodeId":"p:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized","semanticId":"Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.Parameters.pWD_isParameterized"},"s:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.html#s-Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.HierarchyFacts.A_mono:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono:0"],"kind":"statement","label":"Statement 1: Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono","nodeId":"s:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono","semanticId":"Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.A_mono"},"s:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.html#s-Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.HierarchyFacts.W_mono:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono:0"],"kind":"statement","label":"Statement 8: Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono","nodeId":"s:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono","semanticId":"Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_mono"},"s:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_subset_FPT_of_hard":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.html#s-Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_subset_FPT_of_hard","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.WHierarchy.HierarchyFacts.W_subset_FPT_of_hard:conclusion:Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_subset_FPT_of_hard:0"],"kind":"statement","label":"Statement 9: Lax496464.WH_B5_HierarchyFacts.W_subset_FPT_of_hard","no